cff-version: 1.2.0
message: 'To cite the joinpoint package in publications use:'
type: software
license: GPL-3.0-or-later
title: 'joinpoint: Trend Analysis by Joinpoint Regression'
version: 0.1.0
date-released: '2026-10-10'
abstract: >-
  Fits joinpoint (segmented line) regression models for trend analysis of
  rates, proportions, counts and other series. Joinpoints are located by an
  exhaustive grid search and the number of joinpoints is selected by the
  weighted Bayesian information criterion, BIC, BIC3, modified BIC, data
  dependent selection, the sequential permutation test or a Monte Carlo
  likelihood ratio test. Provides annual percent change (APC) and average
  annual percent change (AAPC) estimates with parametric and empirical
  quantile confidence intervals, heteroscedastic and autocorrelated error
  options, Poisson and logistic joinpoint models, covariate adjustment,
  continuous joinpoints, jump and comparability ratio models, pairwise
  comparisons of trends, clustering of contiguous age groups, age adjustment,
  and ggplot2 graphics.
